Italy in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (hilltop huts, amphitheatre and aqueduct, broken columns, ribbed dome and bell tower, a telescope and Jupiter's moons,
a mosaic over an arcade, a piazza with fountain and scooters, a lagoon city with gondolas) are original stylised silhouettes
drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): a mandolin by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
accordion reeds, tamburello and drums synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, wind, birds, crows, crowd, crickets, river, fountain, town hum: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
